QuestGuidance.Register("en",57,{
[1793]="70059E00\n1\tDeliver a missive to Fregi at Erebor\030Deliver a missive to Garni at Erebor\030Deliver a missive to Skalla at Erebor\030Deliver a missive to Uddvar at Erebor\030Deliver a missive to Vísbur at Erebor\tKing Thorin's riders can be found at the Lonely Mountain, Erebor. King Thorin has asked you to deliver missives to his riders at Erebor. You should deliver missives to King Thorin's riders.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor\tKing Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor. You have delivered all of the missives to King Thorin's riders at Erebor. You should return to King Thorin.\n",
[1794]="70059DFA\n1\tTalk to Hersegg and learn of 'Nár's Tale'\tHersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. Hersegg has offered to tell you Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.\n2\tTalk to Hersegg at Akrâz-zahar\tHersegg can be found at Akrâz-zahar in Erebor, the Lonely Mountain. You have listened to Hersegg's telling of Nár's tale as transcribed by her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer. You should talk to Hersegg.\n3\tBegin your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar (Use 'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' in Akrâz-zahar to travel to Azanulbizar, T.A. 2799)\t'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' can be found at Akrâz-zahar within the Lonely Mountain. After learning that King Thorin wishes for you to learn more of the Battle of Azanulbizar, Hersegg has directed you to the works of her grandfather, Hermáth Stormhammer, collected in a volume known as 'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar'.\n4\tComplete your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar\t'Tales of Yore: Azanulbizar' can be found at Akrâz-zahar within the Lonely Mountain. You have begun your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should complete your study before returning to King Thorin. NOTE: You must complete the deed 'The Battle of Azanulbizar' to advance this quest.\n5\tTalk to King Thorin in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor\tKing Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor. You have finished your study of Hermáth Stormhammer's account of the Battle of Azanulbizar. You should return to King Thorin.\n",
[1795]="70059DFF\n1\tTalk to King Thorin\tKing Thorin can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain at Erebor. King Thorin has asked you to accompany him to Vosh Torú for a meeting with one of the Kharum-ubnâr. You should talk to King Thorin.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin at Vosh Torú\tKing Thorin can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain. After talking with King Thorin, Hermáth Stormhammer has agreed to aid Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to King Thorin.\n3\tTalk to Hersegg at Vosh Torú\tHersegg can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain. As King Thorin left Vosh Torú, Hersegg called you over. You should talk to Hersegg.\n4\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Vosh Torú\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain. In an effort to aid King Thorin, Hermáth Stormhammer has agreed to travel to Elderslade and join Prince Durin and the Gabil'akkâ in the reclamation of Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n5\tLeave Vosh Torú and await Hermáth Stormhammer in the Dwelling-halls\tVosh Torú can be found in the Lonely Mountain. Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to wait outside Vosh Torú as he equips himself. You should leave Vosh Torú and wait outside.\n6\tWait for Hermáth Stormhammer outside Vosh Torú\tYou should wait for Hermáth Stormhammer outside Vosh Torú.\n7\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found outside Vosh Torú in the Lonely Mountain. Hermáth Stormhammer has equipped himself, and it appears Hersegg has convinced him to let her join the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[1796]="70067F3C\n1\tAyaluk is concerned that the overseer in Rakhatâb has injured or killed his brother Zûfan.\t\n2\tSpeak with Ayaluk in Rakhatâb\tYou discovered that there was a missing pack, oil lantern, and trail rations taken from the home.\n3\tFind Ayaluk's brother Zûfan\tZûfan likely went to the place where the siblings used to hide as children, north from the city and then west along the cliffs near the shoreline. Go there and ensure that the brother is well.\n4\tWitness the tragedy\tZûfan likely went to the place where the siblings used to hide as children, north from the city and then west along the cliffs near the shoreline. Go there and ensure that the brother is well.\n5\tBring the sad news to Ayaluk in Rakhatâb\tUlanor found Zûfan before you and exacted the blood price for his debts. You need to deliver this sad news to Ayaluk.\n",
[1797]="70067F4F\n1\tSpeak with Foreman Nûrut\tAyaluk asked that you return to the foreman and express his heartfelt thanks.\n2\tFind and speak with Nûrut\tThe foreman was not at his post. Where could he have gone? You hear a nearby whisper that there is a new overseer; perhaps you should go and check.\n",
[1798]="70047BD5\n1\tSearch the Dead Marshes for the spear that slew Faramir\tThe spear can be found somewhere in the southern reaches of the Dead Marshes. Faramir has asked you to seek the Wainrider spear that slew him in the Dead Marshes in the hope that it might grant you passage into Dol Acharn.\n2\tDeliver the spearhead to Faramir near Dol Acharn\tFaramir can be found near the foot of Dol Acharn. You have recovered the remains of the Wainrider spearhead and should now return it to Faramir.\n",
[1799]="70045221\n1\tDefeat the Black Serpent\030Defeat the Princes of Harad\030Defeat Jarl Dauthar\tThe Black Serpent rallies the Men of Harad to greater viciousness as the many forces of Sauron move against Minas Tirith. In addition to his sons, the strongest of the Enemy's forces creep onto the field in search of you and your fellows.\n",
[1800]="70045251\n1\tDefeat the Black Serpent\030Defeat the Princes of Harad\030Defeat Jarl Dauthar\tThe Black Serpent rallies the Men of Harad to greater viciousness as the many forces of Sauron move against Minas Tirith. In addition to his sons, the strongest of the Enemy's forces creep onto the field in search of you and your fellows.\n",
[1801]="70041869\n1\tMalthellim's folk can be found throughout Ost Anglebed. Steward Malthellim has asked you to speak to the people of Ost Anglebed about the various rumours surrounding the Heirs of Castamir.\t\n2\tTalk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed\tNimithil can be found in the lowest section of Ost Anglebed with her guards. You have spoken to many folk of Ost Anglebed and should now seek out Nimithil.\n",
[1802]="7004E493\n1\tSeal leaks in Járnfast (total: 8)\tLeaks can be found throughout Járnfast. Holkur has asked you to aid the Dwarves of the Iron Hills in sealing leaks from the underground source of the River Carnen in Járnfast.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have sealed many leaks within Járnfast.\n",
[1803]="70052B1E\n1\tCollect handfuls of beckberries (total: 8)\tBeckberry bushes can be found on the islet of Avabárg. Hoping to ward off illness and regain his youthful strength, Germund has asked you to seek out beckberries on the islet of Avabárg.\n2\tDeliver the beckberries to Germund\tGermund can be found in Hultvís. You have gathered several handfuls of beckberries and should now deliver them to Germund.\n",
[1804]="7003E2FB\n1\tDefeat Blood-eye\tBlood-eye roams the south-eastern fields of Fornost. You should defeat Blood-eye and his pack of barghests.\n2\tDefeat Blood-eye\tBlood-eye roams the south-eastern fields of Fornost. You should defeat Blood-eye and his pack of barghests.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the evil Blood-eye, silencing the chilling howls that haunt the southern Fields of Fornost.\n",
[1805]="700084CB\n1\tChallenge the Silk-lady\tThe Silk-lady is in the Angmarim fortress of Bail Boglakh on the north side of Malenhad, which guards the road into eastern Angmar. Lornë has asked you and your companions to confront the Silk-lady at the high tower therein, in hopes of finding and freeing her sister Muirnë.\n2\tReturn to Lornë and tell her of Muirnë's fate\tYou confronted the Silk-lady and learned that she was in fact Lornë's sister Muirnë. You defeated the Silk-lady in combat and now must bear the dark tidings back to Lornë. Lornë can be found at Tyrn Lhuig in Malenhad.\n",
[1806]="70022484\n1\tCollect blood-stained runes (total: 6)\tFell spirits and their Angmarim masters can be found in Ost Elendil, beyond the bridge of Ariant. You should defeat the fell spirits inside Ost Elendil and collect the blood-stained runes used by the Angmarim there to command them.\n",
[1807]="7002EE63\n1\tFind a veteran of many battles somewhere in the East Wall who can shed light on the bloodstained tree\tIf you are able to find a veteran of many battles and combats in war somewhere in the East Wall, he may be able to shed some light on what happened at the Dead Orc Glade.\n",
[1808]="70008347\n1\tCollect dull bloodstones (total: 8)\tThe hill-beasts of Fasach-larran often carry bloodstones they find on the ground. Many of the creatures make their home in Nád Nathair, north of Aughaire. Lakhina has asked you to defeat hill-beasts and recover the dull bloodstones they often carry.\n2\tBring the dull bloodstones to Lakhina\tLakhina is at the centre island of Aughaire, east of Crannog's ruling-seat. You have collected dull bloodstones from hill-beasts in Fasach-larran and should now return them to Lakhina.\n",
[1809]="7003E2F6\n1\tDefeat Achassoth\tAchassoth can be found in the central Fields of Fornost, north of the road leading west towards Evendim. You should defeat Achassoth, for this being has sapped the warmth from the Fields of Fornost.\n2\tDefeat Achassoth\tAchassoth can be found in the central Fields of Fornost, north of the road leading west towards Evendim. You should defeat Achassoth, for this being has sapped the warmth from the Fields of Fornost.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated one of the chief forces of evil in the Fields of Fornost.\n",
[1810]="7000835B\n1\tDefeat Bloodwing\030Defeat drakes in Nád Nathair (total: 14)\tBloodwing rules her brood of drakes from the summit of the cliffs of Nád Nathair, above the lower slopes where hill-beasts roam. Nád Nathair is north of Aughaire, in Fasach-larran. Cuinthorn told you of Bloodwing, a mighty drake who has claimed the lives of many great heroes, and wondered if you and your allies would be the ones to end her reign.\n2\tTalk to Cuinthorn\tCuinthorn is in the Búth Sánkhas of Aughaire, south-east of the market. Cuinthorn is waiting to hear of your success against Bloodwing and her brood of drakes.\n",
[1811]="7002824E\n1\tDefeat Dievlig in the Bonevales (total: 8)\030Collect sigils (total: 3)\tThe Dievlig patrol can be found upon the hill north of Echad Naeglanc. Naeglanc has asked you to defeat the remnant of the patrol which attacked him and his allies and bring him their sigils.\n2\tTalk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales\tNaeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, south of the hill where you fought the Dievlig patrol. You should bring the sigils you collected to Naeglanc with news of your victory.\n",
[1812]="70058E15\n1\tTalk to Penfold\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold, tiers 1-5 raid deeds.\n",
[1813]="7003EA76\n1\tCollect the rare flower\tThe rare flower grows in the Blooming Fens along the Bruinen. Canaddal has asked you to collect a rare flower to make medicine for the visiting travellers.\n2\tBring the rare flower to Canaddal\tCanaddal is posted at the head of the path leading into the High Moor, high above the Blooming Fens. You should bring the flower you collected to Canaddal at once.\n",
[1814]="70025973\n1\tUse the glass forge (total: 3)\tThe glass forge is next to Mundaric Sandheaver in Dwaling. Mundaric Sandheaver has asked you to use the forge to blow some glass.\n2\tTalk to Mundaric Sandheaver in Dwaling\tMundaric Sandheaver is at Dwaling. Mundaric Sandheaver will be interested to hear how your first glass-blowing experience went.\n",
[1815]="7003A4CB\n1\tBurn Rashat-hai banners\tYou have discovered banners adorned with crude depictions of the Dead Men of Dunharrow.\n2\tBurn Rashat-hai banners (total: 8)\tRashat-hai banners can be found throughout Gurz-shâpol. You have discovered banners adorned with crude depictions of the Dead Men of Dunharrow, and should burn them before the Orcs can fly them in Kingstead.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have burned many banners in Gurz-shâpol, and prevented the Orcs from flying their standards in Kingstead.\n",
[1816]="70001857\n1\tDefeat the Ongbúrz Chieftain\tThe Ongbúrz camp is south-west of Esteldín across the Kingsfell. You should slay the Orc-chieftain in hopes that his death will throw the Ongbúrz into disarray.\n2\tDefeat Ongbúrz Chieftain\tThe Ongbúrz camp is south-west of Esteldín across the Kingsfell. You should slay the Orc-chieftain in hopes that his death will throw the Ongbúrz into disarray.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Ongbúrz Chieftain, a cruel Orc who stood at the head of Gurzlum's might.\n",
[1817]="7006840B\n1\tCollect boar hides ([see journal]/12)\030Collect boar haunches ([see journal]/12)\tAbido asked that you make your way throughout the eastern Cape of Umbar in search of boars to collect their hides and meat.\n2\tDeliver the haunches and hides to Abido at the hunter's expedition camp\tYou collected hides and haunches from the boars in the wilds of eastern Cape of Umbar. Deliver the haunches and hides to Abido at the hunter's expedition camp in south-eastern Cape of Umbar.\n",
[1818]="70006500\n1\tDefeat Brandy-hills Swine\tcreate entity/npc/mn_boar/mn_boar_brandyhills_brokentusk.wc and kill it\n2\tGo see [see journal]\t\n",
[1819]="70007CD9\n1\tBring the Perfect Boar-tusk to an Elf weaponsmith in Rivendell\tA weaponsmith in Rivendell might be able to craft the boar-tusk you obtained into a deadly weapon. Rivendell might be the home of a weaponsmith able to work with the boar-tusk you obtained.\n",
[1820]="7001B228\n1\tDefeat boars in the north Bree-fields (total: 12)\tBoars can be found throughout the north Bree-fields. Ham Greythistle has asked you to hunt boars for him.\n2\tReturn to Ham Greythistle at Thornley's work-site\tHam Greythistle awaits your return at Thornley's work-site. You should return to Ham Greythistle and inform him of your success.\n",
[1821]="700669B2\n1\tHunt perturbed wild boars in the Farrowfold (total: 5)\tYou have been tasked to hunt boars for food. The boars in question may be found at the Farrowfold, south-west of Cornworth.\n2\tTalk to Branach\tYou have done as Branach asked. Return to him. Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-east of Farrowfold.\n",
[1822]="70017586\n1\tProclaim your prowess in Thorin's Hall\tDwalin's throne is in Thorin's Hall, far to the west of Moria. Valthor has instructed you to go forth and boast of your great deeds before the throne of Dwalin.\n2\tTalk to Thrymur at Thorin's Hall\tThrymur is near Dwalin's throne in Thorin's Hall. Thrymur was not impressed with you. You should speak with him again and proclaim your great deeds.\n3\tTalk to Valthor at the Shadowed Refuge in Moria\tValthor is at the Shadowed Refuge in Khazad-dûm, far to the east of Thorin's Hall. Thrymur told you to return to Valthor in Moria and repeat what you said to him.\n",
[1823]="70040386\n1\tDefeat Corsair boatswains\tCorsair boatswains can be found in their encampment in north-eastern Lamedon. You should defeat boatswains at the Corsair encampment.\n2\tDefeat Corsair boatswains (total: 3)\tCorsair boatswains can be found in their encampment in north-eastern Lamedon. You should defeat boatswains at the Corsair encampment.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of the strong and fearsome boatswains that walk amongst the bold Corsairs invading Lamedon.\n",
[1824]="7006100B\n1\tTalk to Bingo Boffin in Tighfield\tBingo is in Tighfield, and Dinodas believes he might have seen where the other Boffin children went.\n2\tFind Fosco Boffin\tFosco Boffin apparently went in search of Elf-boats on the western rivers of Yondershire.\n3\tTalk to Fosco Boffin by the riverside\tFosco Boffin has found a hobbit-boat in one of the rivers of Yondershire.\n4\tFosco told you that Marigold headed north in the direction of Lhúngobel, seeking enemies to slay.\t\n5\tFosco told you that Marigold headed north in the direction of Lhúngobel, seeking enemies to slay.\t\n6\tTalk to Bingo Boffin at Lhúngobel\tBingo Boffin has followed you to Lhúngobel.\n7\tFind Esmeralda at the dancing competition at Long Cleeve\tBingo heard rumours of a dancing competition happening at Long Cleeve, and thinks that seems a likely place to find Esmeralda.\n8\tTalk to Esmeralda Boffin at Long Cleeve\tEsmeralda Boffin is dancing at Long Cleeve.\n9\tEsmeralda will not return to Nobottle until you perform in her dancing competition. You had better dance!\t\n10\tEsmeralda will not return to Nobottle until you perform in her dancing competition. You had better dance!\t\n11\tTalk to Esmeralda at Long Cleeve\tEsmeralda Boffin is at Long Cleeve, dancing.\n12\tFind Marigold Boffin at the ruins of Bâr Faroth\tEsmeralda saw Marigold heading north in the direction of Bâr Faroth.\n13\tTalk to Nárnaz the Smiter near Bâr Faroth\tNárnaz the Smiter encountered a deadly hobbit-adventurer at Bâr Faroth, to his sorrow.\n14\tTalk to Bingo Boffin at Bâr Faroth\tBingo Boffin has arrived at Bâr Faroth.\n15\tMarigold Boffin went ahead to the Old Links to stop the planned goblin-mischief.\t\n16\tTalk to Berilac on the Old Links\tBerilac slept through the commotion on the Old Links.\n17\tFind Griffo Boffin\tBerilac dreamed of a delicious smell wafting from Northcotton Farm, in the east: just the sort of odour to attract the attention of his hungry sibling Griffo.\n18\tTalk to Griffo Boffin\tGriffo Boffin stands by a waggon bearing food from Northcotton Farm.\n19\tTalk to Dinodas outside 8 Honeymead Lane\tNow that you have found all of his brothers and sisters, you should return to Dinodas outside 8 Honeymead Lane, in Nobottle.\n",
})
